      "content": "The table matcher interprets quotes and parentheses inside JavaScript comments and regex literals as table syntax. For example, a valid `it.each([/\\(/])('title', fn)` is omitted because the regex's `(` is treated as a nested expression; an unmatched apostrophe in a table comment likewise prevents matching. These silent omissions undermine the before/after inventory check. Handle comments and regex literals when scanning table boundaries, and add regression fixtures for both.",
